{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>If a man takes a wife.</b> The pericah is joined [to the preceding one] according to the opinion of the challengers, on account of \"she covered [it] with it.\" But the truth, by way of derash, is that it is joined on account of the house, and afterward the garment, and afterward the mistress of the house:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase 'on account of תכסה בה' reads hyper-literally; the cryptic reference to the preceding pericah's final verse (Deut 22:12, תכסה) is preserved without expansion. 'בעלת הבית' rendered 'mistress of the house' following the chain logic (house → garment → woman)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:22.196185261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}